Attempt 01 did not reach the registered fault injection. It stopped while serializing the first observed X KeyPress because python-xlib KeyPress objects expose `window`, not `event`:

AttributeError: event
  candidate.py, wait_event: event.event

The session was terminated only by the harness finally block; this is not a session-parent SIGKILL result and is excluded from the experiment decision. The adapter now records `event.window.id`, covered by `test_x_event_record_uses_window_id_without_server_event_attribute`.
